  "Question": "A car travels at a constant speed of 60 km/h. Its travel time \\(t\\) (h) and distance \\(s\\) (km) satisfy \\(s=60t\\). Which of the following is the constant?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(s\\)",
    "B": "\\(t\\)",
    "C": "\\(60\\)",
    "D": "\\(s\\) and \\(t\\)"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The speed is fixed at 60 during uniform motion, so it is a constant. The distance \\(s\\) and time \\(t\\) both change, so they are variables.",
